{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>At the entrance of the tent of meeting you shall sit.</b> To mention, and you shall not die." "<b>I have commanded.</b> A verb whose noun form is not called. Some say: כן צויתי אתכם (\"so I have commanded you\"). And if he did not specify, the phrase refers to sitting at the entrance of the tent of meeting."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "Resolved the unspecified pronoun 'he' as Moses; 'the phrase' refers back to the verse's command to sit at the tent of meeting."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:08.766990634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}